[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Trapped in a Mine]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.10]Why is the rescue taking so long? | 为什么营救花费这么长时间？
[00:15.18]Six men have been trapped in a mine for seventeen hours. | 6个人被困在矿井里已有17个小时了。
[00:21.12]If they are not brought to the surface soon they may lose their lives. | 如果不尽快把他们救到地面上来，他们就有可能丧生。
[00:26.79]However, rescue operations are proving difficult. | 然而事实证明营救工作非常困难。
[00:31.65]If explosives are used, vibrations will cause the roof of the mine to collapse. | 如果用炸药，震动会使矿井顶塌下来。
[00:38.73]Rescue workers are therefore drilling a hole on the north side of the mine. | 因此营救人员在矿井北侧钻孔。
[00:45.14]They intend to bring the men up in a special capsule. | 他们打算用一种特制的容器把人救上来。
[00:50.09]If there had not been a hard layer of rock beneath the soil, | 如果不是土壤下面有一层坚硬的岩石，
[00:55.15]they would have completed the job in a few hours. | 他们几个小时就可以完成这项工作。
[00:59.64]As it is, they have been drilling for 16 hours and they still have a long way to go. | 实际上他们已钻了16个小时，但离凿通还有很长一段路。
[01:08.62]Meanwhile, a microphone, which was lowered into the mine two hours ago, | 与此同时，两个小时前放下去的一台麦克风
[01:15.18]has enabled the men to keep in touch with their closest relatives. | 使井下的人得以与其最亲近的亲属保持联系。
[01:20.74]Though they are running out of food and drink, | 虽然他们的食物和饮料都快消耗殆尽了，
[01:24.18]the men are cheerful and confident that they will get out soon. | 但他们情绪很高，确信很快就会获救。
[01:29.90]They have been told that rescue operations are progressing smoothly. | 他们被告知营救工作进行得很顺利。
[01:35.41]If they knew how difficult it was to drill through the hard rock, they would lose heart. | 如果他们知道钻透坚硬的岩石有多么困难，他们就会丧失信心。
